---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import AnonymizeChatText from '@/components/tools/redact/text/AnonymizeChatText.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="anonymize-chat-text" width="wide">
  <AnonymizeChatText client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to use it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Export the chat from the app, or copy the messages.</li>
      <li>Drop the file on the box or paste the text. The tool finds the line format and lists the people who wrote.</li>
      <li>Each person gets one fake name. It replaces their name as sender and every time someone mentions them.</li>
      <li>Check the result. Press a mark to keep a value. Add missed nicknames to the always-hide list.</li>
      <li>Copy the result or download it as a .txt file.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Supported exports</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>WhatsApp: Export chat, Without media. Both the iPhone and the Android line formats work.</li>
      <li>Telegram: the JSON or HTML export from Telegram Desktop, or copied messages.</li>
      <li>Slack: the JSON files of a workspace export, or copied messages. User IDs in mentions are replaced too.</li>
      <li>Discord: text or JSON exports, or copied messages.</li>
      <li>Teams, Signal, iMessage and plain transcripts with "Name: message" lines.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The line formats are read with pattern rules. Phone numbers, emails, addresses, card and bank numbers are found with
      pattern rules too. A language model finds the names of people who are mentioned but did not write. The model and its
      runtime download once from this site (about 35 MB) and stay in your browser's storage.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>
      Open the Network tab in your browser's developer tools and paste the chat. Apart from the model files on the first
      use, the page makes no requests. After the first use the tool also works with the network turned off.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Nicknames and names written in lower case can be missed. Add them to the always-hide list.</li>
      <li>Names inside photos, voice notes and attachments are not part of a text export and are not changed.</li>
      <li>The fake names are new for each visit. Download the result if you need the same names again.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
